**Approved. No new defects found.** The round-7 corrections are present and covered by passing focused tests, including the race-enabled run.

`go vet`, strict artifact-check and strict surface-check passed. Artifact-check emitted provenance warnings; surface-check reported zero findings. Review-check and closeout-check remain pending approval and lifecycle completion. Full validation uses the supplied sealed evidence. The repository is unchanged; no attestation was recorded.

Applied rules: backend-go, security, documentation-style and delivery-evidence. Reviewed the knowledge guidance and B34 handoff.

The design addresses offset drift by binding a signed continuation to its query and ordered collection, then refusing changed collections. Process-local keys and recomputation are sufficient for the selected restart strategy; persistent snapshots would become justified if cross-restart continuation or indexed reads became requirements. Accepted limitations remain full-scan cost, restart invalidation and weaker metadata detection outside Linux. Cross-platform behavior was not independently exercised.

`SD-5c6c5a14` maps to D1 and R1–R8: the ADR records the token contract, restart strategy, bounds, costs and compatibility decisions.

